WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.711
<i>It seems today ♪</i>

00:02.711 --> 00:04.587
<i>That all you see ♪</i>

00:04.671 --> 00:08.133
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.133 --> 00:12.262
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:12.262 --> 00:14.389
<i>On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.389 --> 00:18.226
<i>Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.226 --> 00:21.521
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.521 --> 00:23.106
<i>All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.106 --> 00:24.441
<i>Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.441 --> 00:30.071
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:31.072 --> 00:32.741
Hi, I'm Peter Griffin.

00:32.741 --> 00:34.576
It's almost Oscar night.

00:34.576 --> 00:36.995
Boy, we've lost so many greats this year,

00:36.995 --> 00:38.955
including a dead costume designer

00:39.039 --> 00:40.540
who will get spill-over applause

00:40.540 --> 00:43.543
from the photo of Sean Connery
that directly precedes him.

00:43.543 --> 00:46.463
Tonight, we salute
some past Best Picture winners,

00:46.463 --> 00:48.757
whichever ones I spin on this wheel.

00:54.679 --> 00:56.473
The wheel has spoken!

00:56.473 --> 00:58.183
<i>The Silence of the Lambs.</i>

01:04.773 --> 01:08.359
Ah... what a beautiful day
to not get bodily fluids

01:08.443 --> 01:10.361
thrown in your face and hair.

01:10.445 --> 01:14.657
And now, for some rock tunes
to pump me up.

01:14.741 --> 01:17.077
<i>One, two princes kneel before you... ♪</i>

01:17.077 --> 01:20.413
Oh, right, 'cause it's the early '90s.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.332
Vaulting over a log.

01:22.332 --> 01:24.084
Jumping a water hazard.

01:24.084 --> 01:26.336
Climbing up a cargo net.

01:26.336 --> 01:28.379
Becoming an FBI agent is basically

01:28.463 --> 01:30.924
like being on <i>Battle of the Network Stars.</i>

01:30.924 --> 01:33.551
<i>You rockets ain't in... ♪</i>

01:38.389 --> 01:40.391
- Aah!
- Agent Starling.

01:40.475 --> 01:41.601
Good to see you.

01:41.601 --> 01:43.353
Wh-Why is your face so big?

01:43.353 --> 01:45.855
Oh, this movie
is mostly extreme close-ups.

01:45.939 --> 01:47.816
Oh. Yeah. Weird.

01:47.816 --> 01:49.776
Anyway, sorry you had to come so quickly,

01:49.776 --> 01:52.153
but this thing with no timetable
couldn't wait.

01:52.237 --> 01:55.115
We need you to talk
to a super smart psychopath.

01:55.115 --> 01:56.574
How smart?

01:56.658 --> 01:58.076
Like, he can do
the <i>New York Times</i> crossword

01:58.076 --> 01:59.244
through Thursday.

01:59.244 --> 02:01.412
Friday, he can maybe get a corner or two.

02:01.496 --> 02:03.081
So, what's the job?

02:03.081 --> 02:04.666
Fancy creep, eats people.

02:04.666 --> 02:06.543
- Talk to him.
- Got it.

02:06.543 --> 02:08.461
And this is a big deal,
'cause you're a woman.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.171
We're not gonna say it's a big deal,

02:10.255 --> 02:12.465
but everyone watching
will know it's a big deal

02:12.549 --> 02:13.758
'cause of the time period,

02:13.842 --> 02:15.343
even though a man is helping you.

02:15.343 --> 02:16.803
Now run along, toots.

02:22.559 --> 02:24.269
So, you're in the FBI, huh?

02:24.269 --> 02:26.104
Me too.

02:26.104 --> 02:28.481
Got this bad boy in Venice Beach.

02:30.066 --> 02:31.943
Okay, all right.

02:31.943 --> 02:33.653
You can talk to Lecter now.

02:40.493 --> 02:42.495
Hello, Clarice.

02:42.579 --> 02:44.831
Dr. Lecter, I need your help.

02:44.831 --> 02:47.917
Nope, nope, nope.
I'll only help if there's a quid pro quo.

02:48.001 --> 02:49.711
 Okay, what is it?

02:49.711 --> 02:53.840
I want Mario Lopez to record
my outgoing voice mail message.

02:53.840 --> 02:55.675
What?! You're insane!

02:55.675 --> 02:59.012
He's a huge star
at this specific sliver of time.

02:59.012 --> 03:01.598
Figure it out. Those are my terms.

03:06.728 --> 03:10.648
Sorry, these Capri Suns
are notoriously difficult to open.

03:12.734 --> 03:15.737
<i>Yeah, one, two... ♪</i>

03:17.155 --> 03:18.990
: <i>That's what I said now ♪</i>

03:18.990 --> 03:20.450
<i>Princes... ♪</i>

03:27.498 --> 03:28.833
You need some help?

03:28.917 --> 03:30.084
Yeah, thanks.

03:30.168 --> 03:33.504
I can't seem to get
this giant 1991 computer

03:33.588 --> 03:35.673
into the back of my van.

03:35.757 --> 03:39.594
Careful, I had it on
for 20 minutes, so it's very hot.

03:44.933 --> 03:47.185
Okay, I got what you asked for.

03:47.185 --> 03:48.853
<i>Hey, this is Mario Lopez</i>

03:48.937 --> 03:50.355
<i>letting you know that Hannibal Lecter</i>

03:50.355 --> 03:51.814
<i>can't get to the phone right now,</i>

03:51.898 --> 03:53.441
<i>so please leave a message.</i>

03:53.441 --> 03:55.235
<i>And now, I think
I'm about to be saved by the...</i>

03:56.361 --> 03:57.570
Not good enough!

03:57.654 --> 03:59.447
I wanted him to record it as Slater.

03:59.447 --> 04:01.532
What?! You never said that.

04:01.616 --> 04:03.117
It should've been understood.

04:03.201 --> 04:04.827
Don't test me, Starling.

04:04.911 --> 04:06.621
A census taker did that once,

04:06.621 --> 04:09.040
and I ate his liver with dry Cheerios

04:09.040 --> 04:11.042
and a mashed-up banana.

04:13.086 --> 04:15.463
Sorry, I'm just a little nervous.

04:15.463 --> 04:17.173
When I was a girl,

04:17.257 --> 04:18.591
I went to live on my uncle's farm,

04:18.675 --> 04:21.803
and I heard these lambs screaming,

04:21.803 --> 04:23.554
screaming as they were being slaughtered.

04:23.638 --> 04:25.473
It was horrible.

04:25.473 --> 04:28.268
And I want to thank
Alan Weiss at William Morris.

04:28.268 --> 04:31.271
Also, my high school drama teacher,
Lucas Wohl.

04:31.271 --> 04:33.982
Oh, they were just
killing those poor lambs.

04:33.982 --> 04:35.316
I wanted to save them, but I couldn't.

04:35.400 --> 04:38.194
And, Mandy and Jenny
at home, go to bed, kids.

04:38.278 --> 04:39.821
Mommy did it!

04:39.821 --> 04:42.073
I am coming home with one of these!

04:50.999 --> 04:53.501
CVS brand lotion?

04:53.501 --> 04:56.170
It's the same ingredients as Nivea.

04:57.255 --> 05:00.133
It puts the off-brand lotion on its skin,

05:00.133 --> 05:02.844
or else it gets the hose again.

05:02.844 --> 05:04.595
The top isn't even a pump.

05:04.679 --> 05:06.848
You're paying for the pump!

05:13.980 --> 05:15.857
Dr. Lecter, we are running out of time.

05:15.857 --> 05:17.775
I need you to give me some clue,

05:17.859 --> 05:20.194
anything that might
lead me in the right direction.

05:20.278 --> 05:23.239
His name's Buffalo Bill,
heavyset blond kid

05:23.323 --> 05:25.742
who lives in that crappy place
behind McDonald's.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.160
Hmm.

05:27.160 --> 05:28.453
I'll have to really lean

05:28.453 --> 05:30.455
on my budding criminology skills

05:30.455 --> 05:33.082
to decipher these obscure breadcrumbs.

06:12.163 --> 06:13.748
Coming up, dinner.

06:13.748 --> 06:16.626
But first, I turn my back
to a dangerous murderer.

06:28.888 --> 06:31.391
Oh, hey, Sarge.
Your wife called and said it was urgent.

06:31.391 --> 06:33.226
Oh, uh, okay.

06:33.226 --> 06:35.937
Yeah, she sounded very not happy.

06:35.937 --> 06:37.605
You need to call her back ASAP.

06:37.605 --> 06:38.815
Got it, thanks.

06:38.815 --> 06:41.651
Starting to think I did this guy a favor.

06:48.449 --> 06:51.494
It puts its finger on the doorbell.

06:51.494 --> 06:53.037
We're looking for someone.

06:53.121 --> 06:54.497
Have you seen her?

06:54.497 --> 06:58.626
Oh, wait, is she that
great, big, huge, plump,

06:58.626 --> 07:02.004
very large, Rubenesque,
fat girl who went missing?

07:02.088 --> 07:03.506
Yes, she is rather heavy,

07:03.506 --> 07:05.883
and as you can see,
not particularly attractive.

07:05.967 --> 07:07.718
We've had reports that her personality

07:07.802 --> 07:09.262
is quite grating as well.

07:09.262 --> 07:11.472
I can still hear you guys!

07:31.492 --> 07:33.828
I'm not loving this night vision setting.

07:33.828 --> 07:37.790
Maybe I should
try <i>Night at the Roxbury</i> vision.

07:43.796 --> 07:46.257
- You? Me? You?
- <i>What is love? ♪</i>
- Aah!

07:47.925 --> 07:51.554
It puts the bullet in the fat guy.

07:55.558 --> 07:58.060
And, for having successfully
scaled a cargo net

07:58.144 --> 08:01.522
and connecting two note cards
with a piece of red string,

08:01.606 --> 08:06.152
Clarice Starling,
you are now officially a lady FBI.

08:16.162 --> 08:17.538
You should probably answer that.

08:17.622 --> 08:20.082
I mean, you're the closest thing
to a secretary in here.

08:21.083 --> 08:22.793
Ugh.

08:22.877 --> 08:26.339
Hello, FBI. This is Clarice speaking.

08:26.339 --> 08:27.882
Hello, Clarice.

08:27.882 --> 08:30.468
I just wanted to let you know
that I respect you,

08:30.468 --> 08:32.929
and how important it is
that you're a woman.

08:32.929 --> 08:35.181
Thank you for saying so, Doctor.

08:35.181 --> 08:36.516
'Cause if you were a man,

08:36.516 --> 08:38.768
I would definitely
be captured or dead by now.

08:38.768 --> 08:41.312
- Oh, I...
- Like, if you're Clint Eastwood, I'm dead.

08:41.312 --> 08:44.023
- Harrison Ford? Dead.
- Well, Doctor, I've really got...

08:44.023 --> 08:46.234
You know, I'm not betting
against the <i>Twin Peaks</i> guy--

08:46.234 --> 08:47.777
what's his name? Creepy white guy.

08:47.777 --> 08:50.279
- Kyle MacLachlan.
- Kyle MacLachlan, right.

08:50.363 --> 08:51.531
How do I keep forgetting that?

08:51.531 --> 08:53.866
It's like in my top five dude names.
I have a list.

08:53.950 --> 08:56.494
- Dr. Lecter, I really have to go.
- So do I.

09:00.248 --> 09:03.084
I'm having an old friend for dinner.

09:03.084 --> 09:04.919
Y-You're gonna eat a friend?

09:04.919 --> 09:06.504
That was kind of
supposed to be the last line,

09:06.504 --> 09:07.755
and you ruined it.

09:07.755 --> 09:09.674
I'm gonna say it again
and then hang up quickly.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.135
I'm having an old friend for dinner.

09:13.219 --> 09:14.178
<i>What?!</i>

09:14.262 --> 09:16.055
Oh, my God, this bitch.

09:21.561 --> 09:23.854
<i>My name is...</i>

09:23.938 --> 09:26.649
<i>whatever Kevin Spacey's name was
in this movie.</i>

09:26.649 --> 09:28.526
<i>I bet you think behind that door is</i>

09:28.526 --> 09:30.152
<i>a happy, all-American family.</i>

09:30.236 --> 09:31.153
<i>Nope.</i>

09:31.237 --> 09:32.530
<i>Just me in the shower</i>

09:32.530 --> 09:34.532
<i>with Johnson & Johnson and Johnson.</i>

09:34.532 --> 09:36.742
<i>There were some tears.</i>

09:36.826 --> 09:39.078
<i>That's my wife out there, cutting roses.</i>

09:39.078 --> 09:41.831
<i>Oh, just a heads-up,
there's a ton of roses in this.</i>

09:41.831 --> 09:44.375
<i>I guess they're
supposed to mean something. (sighs)</i>

09:44.375 --> 09:45.793
<i>You know, when I agreed to this,</i>

09:45.793 --> 09:48.004
<i>I 100% thought it was</i> American Pie.

09:48.004 --> 09:50.089
<i>Always read the second word of the title</i>

09:50.089 --> 09:51.424
<i>before you sign something.</i>

09:51.424 --> 09:54.218
Oh, hi, Carolyn. We're your gay neighbors.

09:54.302 --> 09:56.137
That's right, and we're
the only happy people

09:56.137 --> 09:57.638
in the entire film.

09:57.722 --> 09:58.889
<i>Oh, that's the other thing.</i>

09:58.973 --> 10:00.558
<i>This movie really wants you to know</i>

10:00.558 --> 10:03.185
<i>that traditional families
are the messed-up ones.</i>

10:03.269 --> 10:04.687
<i>If you don't want two hours of that,</i>

10:04.687 --> 10:06.272
<i>go turn on</i> The Matrix.

10:06.272 --> 10:07.857
<i>Aw, why aren't we doing that?</i>

10:07.857 --> 10:09.191
Have a great day,

10:09.275 --> 10:11.485
two-dimensional '90s gay neighbors.

10:11.569 --> 10:14.864
- Who are both named Jim.
- Right, who are both named Jim.

10:15.948 --> 10:18.534
- Good morning, my darling.
- Hello, my love.

10:18.618 --> 10:20.870
<i>Keep in mind
that 9/11 hasn't happened yet.</i>

10:20.870 --> 10:22.955
<i>So a strained family dynamic</i>

10:23.039 --> 10:25.166
<i>is still the most dramatic thing there is.</i>

10:25.166 --> 10:28.878
Wow, what a beautiful,
fully heterosexual neighborhood.

10:28.878 --> 10:31.797
Yeah, no. What's up is down here, bro.

10:31.881 --> 10:34.258
Oh, hi, you must be our new neighbors.

10:34.342 --> 10:36.093
I'm Carolyn Burnham,

10:36.177 --> 10:39.055
RE/MAX's top crying realtor in the area.

10:39.055 --> 10:40.973
Uh, thanks, but we just bought a house,

10:41.057 --> 10:42.808
so we don't really need a realtor.

10:45.603 --> 10:47.688
- You don't?
- S-Sorry.

10:47.772 --> 10:49.523
It's okay. You know what?

10:49.607 --> 10:50.816
We'll buy another one.

10:50.900 --> 10:53.152
Oh, great. Great.

10:53.152 --> 10:55.780
Oh, looks like your son and my daughter

10:55.780 --> 10:57.281
are getting to know each other.

10:57.365 --> 11:00.576
Check out this video
I took of a plastic bag.

11:03.996 --> 11:05.831
I'm thinking about sending it in

11:05.915 --> 11:08.042
to <i>America's Funniest Home Videos.</i>

11:08.042 --> 11:10.127
Really? Do you think it's funny enough?

11:10.211 --> 11:13.130
I don't know. I just want to spend $2,000

11:13.214 --> 11:16.842
flying to Los Angeles to maybe win $1,000.

11:21.097 --> 11:23.140
<i>That's halftime.</i>

11:23.224 --> 11:25.351
<i>And now, please welcome
the Suburbia High School</i>

11:25.351 --> 11:28.354
<i>cheer quad, the Dockers Zipper Pushers.</i>

11:40.825 --> 11:42.827
Who is that?

11:56.424 --> 11:58.259
Aah! Aw, damn it. Aw, stop. Stop.

11:58.259 --> 12:01.262
I have seasonal allergies, guys.

12:01.262 --> 12:03.514
<i>All right.</i>

12:03.514 --> 12:04.807
<i>Now the marching band to play</i>

12:04.807 --> 12:07.017
<i>the Suburbia High School fight song.</i>

12:12.106 --> 12:13.733
Geez, again with this song?

12:13.733 --> 12:16.152
Shut up and kiss me, other gay Jim.

12:18.529 --> 12:21.365
Oh, no. No.

12:21.449 --> 12:23.325
I'm very against that.

12:23.409 --> 12:25.286
Remember that for later.

12:25.286 --> 12:27.037
<i>The next day, I quit my job</i>

12:27.121 --> 12:29.373
<i>and was in no way run out of the industry</i>

12:29.457 --> 12:31.083
<i>for groping a busboy in Nantucket.</i>

12:31.167 --> 12:33.169
It was a joke. I was razzing the guy.

12:33.169 --> 12:34.462
Come on.

12:36.422 --> 12:39.759
<i>I got a new job
at a fake movie fast food restaurant.</i>

12:39.759 --> 12:43.179
<i>God, why are movies
so bad at naming restaurants?</i>

12:43.179 --> 12:46.265
Welcome to
Mr. Smiley's BurgerTownVilleLand.

12:46.265 --> 12:48.309
Would you like to try a Large McIntyre?

12:48.309 --> 12:51.645
<i>Yes, my lover and I
will each have adultery burgers.</i>

12:51.729 --> 12:53.606
Second window.

12:56.400 --> 12:59.612
- Two adultery burgers.
- Lester!

12:59.612 --> 13:02.281
Listen, let's not make a big scene here.

13:02.281 --> 13:03.699
We can talk about this when we get...

13:03.783 --> 13:08.537
<i>You</i> don't get to tell <i>me</i>
what to do anymore.

13:09.830 --> 13:11.499
We need more ketchup.

13:11.499 --> 13:14.585
All right, there are some things
you can tell me to do.

13:14.585 --> 13:17.129
<i>After that, I started
lifting weights in my garage.</i>

13:17.213 --> 13:18.714
<i>But I lost track of a spider</i>

13:18.798 --> 13:20.341
<i>that crawled behind the heavy ones,</i>

13:20.341 --> 13:23.052
<i>so I had to use the dainty weights
ladies walk with.</i>

13:23.052 --> 13:24.804
Oh, hey. You got those drugs?

13:24.804 --> 13:26.180
Yep, right here.

13:26.180 --> 13:27.890
Oh, my God.

13:27.890 --> 13:30.309
Look at that plastic bag.

13:30.309 --> 13:32.353
So beautiful.

13:32.353 --> 13:34.688
Do you do a lot of the drugs yourself?

13:34.772 --> 13:36.023
I do, yes.

13:36.023 --> 13:38.234
Okay, let me just get on my knees

13:38.234 --> 13:42.029
and roll a joint at crotch level
like all drug dealers do.

13:42.029 --> 13:44.365
Great, and I'll just lean back,
away from the drugs

13:44.365 --> 13:46.617
like all drug users do.

13:49.036 --> 13:50.830
What the hell?

13:50.830 --> 13:52.289
Am I seeing what I think I'm seeing?

13:52.373 --> 13:53.958
Help me out here, Mr. Furley.

13:53.958 --> 13:56.210
How did this thing win an Oscar?

13:56.210 --> 13:58.712
It's basically <i>Austin Powers.</i>

14:01.799 --> 14:03.759
Yo, yo, check this out.

14:03.843 --> 14:06.512
What if, like, Kramer is just

14:06.512 --> 14:09.056
a figment of Jerry's imagination?

14:09.056 --> 14:12.476
- Wow. Yeah.
-'Cause think about it.

14:12.560 --> 14:16.856
We-we never see him
interacting with anyone else.

14:16.856 --> 14:18.399
Yeah.

14:18.399 --> 14:22.361
Well-well, wait.
I mean, w... Uh, we-we do.

14:22.361 --> 14:25.322
Oh, boy, am I glad you're here.

14:25.406 --> 14:28.325
I don't think I like what I saw earlier.

14:28.409 --> 14:29.702
Oh, was it <i>The Phantom Menace,</i>

14:29.702 --> 14:31.412
which also came out this same year?

14:31.412 --> 14:32.663
Yeah, what a mess.

14:32.663 --> 14:35.666
Ricky, go on home.
I need to talk to Lester.

14:35.666 --> 14:37.543
Aw, I don't want to.

14:37.543 --> 14:39.837
: There's plastic bags.

14:39.837 --> 14:41.714
There are?

14:42.882 --> 14:46.343
Hey, you know how
there's two things we know for sure?

14:46.427 --> 14:49.179
We'll always be able
to bring box cutters on planes,

14:49.263 --> 14:51.807
- and I'm heterosexual?
- Yeah, of course.

14:51.891 --> 14:54.977
Well, turns out only
one of those things is true.

14:54.977 --> 14:56.896
Mm...

14:56.896 --> 14:59.023
Look, I think I gave you the wrong idea

14:59.023 --> 15:02.026
with these pink weights
and pantomiming oral with your son.

15:02.026 --> 15:04.278
- I'm straight.
- I'm so sorry!

15:04.278 --> 15:06.906
I got to go start a megachurch!

15:06.906 --> 15:08.657
Eh, seems right.

15:10.534 --> 15:12.828
Oh, hey, what are you doing here?

15:12.912 --> 15:14.121
I have a flight tomorrow,

15:14.121 --> 15:16.624
and Jane said
I could borrow your box cutter.

15:16.624 --> 15:19.209
Man, I love cutting boxes on planes.

15:19.293 --> 15:23.172
And also-- and this is kind
of embarrassing and unearned--

15:23.172 --> 15:25.507
but I think you're sexy,

15:25.591 --> 15:27.676
and I want to have sex with you.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.637
Ah, sweet! Let's do this.

15:29.637 --> 15:32.890
I should let you know, I'm a virgin.

15:32.890 --> 15:34.350
Not a deal-breaker.

15:34.350 --> 15:35.976
And I should let you know

15:36.060 --> 15:38.437
I'm Chris Hansen from <i>To Catch a Predator.</i>

15:38.437 --> 15:40.105
Aw, crap. Somebody shoot me.

15:44.151 --> 15:45.444
Sorry, I didn't mean to...

15:45.444 --> 15:47.529
Whoa, you're Chris Hansen!

15:47.613 --> 15:50.866
Hey, what do you do
with all the leftover pedophile pizza?

15:50.950 --> 15:53.035
<i>Well, that was</i> American Beauty.

15:53.035 --> 15:54.662
<i>See you at the Oscars.</i>

15:54.662 --> 15:56.205
<i>I'll be there with my mom.</i>

15:56.205 --> 15:58.791
<i>That's not a big,
obvious sign of something, right?</i>

16:13.347 --> 16:15.849
- How's work, Ralph?
- It's a breeze.

16:17.643 --> 16:20.270
- Give my best to Judy.
- Will do.

16:26.652 --> 16:29.446
Hi, my name's Forrest.

16:29.530 --> 16:30.906
Forrest Gump.

16:30.990 --> 16:33.367
Would it be okay
if I sugarcoat race relations

16:33.367 --> 16:36.078
in the South for the next
two and a half hours?

16:36.078 --> 16:39.331
Honey, I'm a Black woman
in a '90s Hollywood movie,

16:39.415 --> 16:41.667
- that's what I'm here for.
- Great.

16:41.667 --> 16:45.337
My mama always said life
was like a box of Good & Plenty:

16:45.421 --> 16:47.798
most people just throw it away.

16:47.798 --> 16:50.175
<i>One day on the bus to school,</i>

16:50.259 --> 16:52.052
<i>I met Jenny.</i>

16:52.136 --> 16:54.471
<i>She was the love of my life.</i>

16:56.515 --> 16:59.143
Hey, look, it's a guy
with nonstandard legs.

16:59.143 --> 17:01.937
Let's bully and throw
rocks at him and not me.

17:03.022 --> 17:05.399
Run, Forrest, run!

17:06.358 --> 17:07.985
<i>And in a magical moment</i>

17:07.985 --> 17:10.738
<i>whose explanation
I assume was cut for time,</i>

17:10.738 --> 17:13.824
<i>I could suddenly run very fast.</i>

17:13.824 --> 17:15.409
<i>But I happened to do it</i>

17:15.409 --> 17:18.287
<i>in front of the meanest
lifeguard in Alabama.</i>

17:18.287 --> 17:21.874
- No running!
- It's for a movie. God.

17:21.874 --> 17:23.667
<i>I was such a fast runner,</i>

17:23.751 --> 17:26.712
<i>I went on to play college movie football,</i>

17:26.712 --> 17:30.591
<i>where all the tacklers
dive two feet behind you and miss.</i>

17:32.801 --> 17:34.511
After I graduated,

17:34.595 --> 17:37.389
I joined the Army
and got shipped off to war.

17:37.473 --> 17:41.143
<i>Vietnam is where
I met my best friend, Bubba,</i>

17:41.143 --> 17:44.480
<i>who really wanted
to have his own squid fishing boat.</i>

17:44.480 --> 17:46.940
<i>In fact, he knew just about</i>

17:47.024 --> 17:48.901
<i>everything you could do with a squid.</i>

17:48.901 --> 17:51.236
Well, there's calamari...

17:53.322 --> 17:55.032
That's about it.

17:55.032 --> 17:57.576
Ambush!

17:58.744 --> 18:01.163
Oh, my God, Lieutenant Dan!

18:02.748 --> 18:05.167
Damn it, save yourself, Gump.

18:05.167 --> 18:07.878
- Leave me here.
- All right.

18:09.046 --> 18:11.048
<i>Bubba was also shot.</i>

18:11.048 --> 18:13.842
<i>And as always happens when a soldier dies,</i>

18:13.926 --> 18:16.011
<i>we discussed business ideas.</i>

18:16.095 --> 18:19.264
I'm dying, Forrest.

18:19.348 --> 18:21.975
I want you to buy
a squid boat in my honor.

18:22.059 --> 18:25.187
How about a gym
exclusively for big white women?

18:25.187 --> 18:28.982
- There could be machines that...
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

18:29.066 --> 18:32.277
You had me at "big white women."

18:34.196 --> 18:36.740
<i>After I got home from Vietnam,</i>

18:36.824 --> 18:39.535
<i>I got to speak at a generic protest.</i>

18:39.535 --> 18:42.746
There's only one thing
to say about Vietnam:

18:42.830 --> 18:45.916
I had this awesome red stuff
on all my food.

18:45.916 --> 18:47.668
I don't 'member what it's called.

18:47.668 --> 18:50.254
It's not hot sauce, but it's not ketchup.

18:50.254 --> 18:52.714
I think it's got a rooster on the label.

18:52.798 --> 18:54.133
Forrest!

18:55.634 --> 18:57.553
Jenny!

18:58.637 --> 18:59.972
Aah! Son of a bitch!

18:59.972 --> 19:03.350
See, guys? This is why no running.

19:03.350 --> 19:05.602
<i>And then--
I know, it's still not over yet--</i>

19:05.686 --> 19:08.021
<i>I bought a squid boat.</i>

19:08.105 --> 19:10.399
<i>Lieutenant Dan was also working with me.</i>

19:10.399 --> 19:12.609
<i>And you know who's super helpful on a boat</i>

19:12.693 --> 19:14.736
<i>that's constantly rocking in the water?</i>

19:14.820 --> 19:16.196
<i>A wheelchair guy.</i>

19:16.280 --> 19:18.448
Hey, Forrest, I got our lunches.

19:19.992 --> 19:21.618
Aah!

19:24.454 --> 19:26.498
So after I was rich,

19:26.582 --> 19:29.710
Jenny came back
and had sex with me one time.

19:29.710 --> 19:32.212
Wow, that was great.

19:32.296 --> 19:35.007
Sorry I was naming presidents during.

19:35.007 --> 19:36.758
So, we getting married or what?

19:36.842 --> 19:39.344
You don't want to marry me, Forrest.

19:40.470 --> 19:41.930
Yeah, you're right.

19:42.014 --> 19:44.183
Okay, well, have a good night.

19:44.183 --> 19:46.685
<i>And then, shockingly late in the movie,</i>

19:46.685 --> 19:48.687
<i>I started running again.</i>

19:48.687 --> 19:50.772
<i>Like, across the country.</i>

19:50.856 --> 19:52.107
<i>Several times.</i>

19:52.191 --> 19:53.859
<i>The whole sequence
is a full eight minutes.</i>

19:53.859 --> 19:55.861
<i>I mean, sometimes this whole movie
feels like it was written</i>

19:55.861 --> 19:58.113
<i>by a seven-year-old
who just ate a bunch of candy.</i>

19:58.197 --> 20:00.240
<i>But I checked, it's just a regular guy.</i>

20:00.324 --> 20:02.034
<i>Anyway, at least we were finally</i>

20:02.034 --> 20:04.369
<i>to the time in our nation's history</i>

20:04.453 --> 20:05.746
<i>when I could listen to this.</i>

20:05.746 --> 20:09.166
<i>Princes, princes who adore you. ♪</i>

20:14.588 --> 20:15.714
Forrest!

20:15.714 --> 20:19.051
I brought you chocolates
picked over by strangers.

20:19.051 --> 20:20.886
Forrest, I'm sick.

20:20.886 --> 20:23.722
Sick? With what?

20:23.722 --> 20:26.016
Oh, I did a movie about that once.

20:26.016 --> 20:27.643
It's called <i>Splash.</i>

20:27.643 --> 20:30.562
No, Forrest.

20:30.646 --> 20:33.357
Oh, I thought you said mermaids.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.817
But I did a movie about your thing, too.

20:35.901 --> 20:37.486
But that's not all.

20:37.486 --> 20:39.112
I want you to meet my son.

20:39.196 --> 20:41.698
Six hours in makeup. One line.

20:41.782 --> 20:43.283
You're his father.

20:43.367 --> 20:45.285
Father?

20:45.369 --> 20:47.788
Is he... like me?

20:47.788 --> 20:49.081
Uhp, you died.

20:49.081 --> 20:50.749
And... feather!

21:34.001 --> 21:35.961
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
